  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0073 database is designed to manage user authentication, authorization, and activity tracking for a web application. It consists of 12 tables that work together to store user information, permissions, roles, and activities. The users table stores information about each user, including their name, email, locale, and theme, as well as their group affiliation, verification status, and password. Each user is associated with a group through the group_id foreign key, which references the id column in the groups table. The groups table stores information about each group, including its slug, name, description, and icon. The permissions table stores information about each permission, including its slug, name, conditions, and description. The roles table stores information about each role, including its slug, name, and description. The role_users table associates users with roles, while the permission_roles table associates permissions with roles. The activities table stores information about each activity, including its id, ip address, user id, type, occurred at timestamp, and description. The password_resets and persistences tables store information about password reset requests and persistent tokens, respectively, while the verifications table stores information about user verifications. The sessions table stores information about each user session, including its id, user id, ip address, user agent, payload, and last activity timestamp. The throttles table stores information about IP address throttling, including the type, ip address, request data, and timestamps.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves enhancing a user management system named UserFrosting, built on a PHP-based web framework. UserFrosting distinguishes itself by providing a fully-functional user management application that can be easily extended to meet custom requirements using a modular system known as \"Sprinkles.\" This system addresses the modern development needs by offering a comprehensive set of tools for building scalable applications.\n\n Objectives\nThe primary objective of the project is to provide robust user management features, including user authentication, role-based access control (RBAC), and administrative capabilities for managing users. It aims to deliver a maintainable and extendable framework that follows modern development practices.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Administrators: Manage user accounts, permissions, and roles.\n- Developers: Extend and customize the application using Sprinkles.\n- End Users: Register, log in, and interact with the application.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. User Authentication: \n   - Users can sign in and maintain persistent sessions with a \"remember me\" feature.\n   \n2. Admin User Management:\n   - Administrators can view, search, sort, create, and edit user accounts, including resetting passwords.\n   - Tools are available to enable or disable users and manage user permissions.\n   \n3. Roles and Permissions:\n   - Utilize powerful RBAC to define access rules and manage permissions through a role management interface.\n   \n4. Extensibility:\n   - Implement custom features using modular Sprinkles without altering the core codebase.\n   - Support for themes, plugins, and more.\n   \n5. User Dashboards:\n   - AdminLTE-themed dashboards for providing users with an interactive interface.\n\n6. Activity Tracking:\n   - Log user activities with details such as IP address and activity type.\n   \n7. Password Management:\n   - Support for password resets and verifications with expiration and completion tracking.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n1. Performance:\n   - Optimization through asset bundling with Node.js and caching for templates and routes.\n   \n2. Documentation:\n   - Comprehensive guides explaining the usage, features, and rationale behind the system components.\n   \n3. Maintainability:\n   - Separation of concerns to minimize code complexity and facilitate future upgrades.\n\n4. Scalability:\n   - Designed to accommodate growth and incorporation of additional user roles and permissions without impacting performance.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0073.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0073\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `locale` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `theme` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `group_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `verification_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`group_id`) REFERENCES `groups` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `icon` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `conditions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `slug` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `role_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permission_roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `occurred_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `activities_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_resets` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `persistences` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `persistences_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `verifications` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `verifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sessions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `user_agent` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `payload` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_activity` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sessions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `throttles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `request_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
